# --- Per-student validation evidence ---------------------------------------
# backend/validation/ holds two tracked files: README.md and template.json.
# `mine.json` is neither - it is a copy of the template that
# docs/VALIDATION_REPORT.md and backend/validation/README.md tell the student to
# create and fill in.  It still carries the placeholders ("clip":
# "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_CLIP.mp4", "annotated_by": "YOUR NAME"), so a `git add -A`
# would commit an unsubmitted template that reads, in the history of a
# validation submission, like real evidence.  The file stays on disk: it is the
# student's working copy, and the local run of the comparison script needs it.
backend/validation/mine.json

# The matching report pair that
# `python -m backend.scripts.validate_against_reference --markdown ... --json ...`
# writes.  One student, one clip, one report - same reasoning as mine.json, and
# the same reason the measurement report (docs/validation-measurement.*) *is*
# tracked: that one is generated from the bundled synthetic dataset and is part
# of the evidence anyone can reproduce without a camera.
docs/validation-detector.md
docs/validation-detector.json

# --- Runtime data ---------------------------------------------------------
# Uploaded clips, annotated videos, the SQLite database and the YOLO
# checkpoint.  All of it is local, all of it is regenerable, none of it is
# source.  The demo dataset under backend/demo/ IS tracked: it is what makes
# the test suite and the demo reproducible.
data/
*.pt

